module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_registration_name_model_drifts_from_the_name_the_runner_registers_under

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundOnRung, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, MechanicallyPreventable, StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data a_registration_name_model_drifts_from_the_name_the_runner_registers_under: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_registration_name_model_drifts_from_the_name_the_runner_registers_under" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable }, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundOnRung { rung: MechanicallyPreventable }, ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "the capability of deriving the registration-name grammar once, from the registering wrapper's own name model, so the join (decode_registration_slot and the per-slot connectivity join) and the registrant cannot disagree; today the grammar is declared in gunbc.runner.runner_incarnation and the wrapper that registers is a separate authority checked only by a witness" } },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a runner registers under a name the fleet's join does not model, so the join reads the slot as unregistered while GitHub holds registrations for it. The model named a slot's registration by the slot's own name (srv1-02); the just-in-time wrapper registers <slot>-<epoch>-<pid>, a new name per incarnation.",

    "HARM, 2026-11-04: 133 offline registrations for srv1-02 accumulated, each a dead incarnation. A join keyed on the slot name found none of them, so a live slot read as orphaned or detached, and the capacity plan either counted a dead incarnation as a population member or refused the whole roster as Foreign. A per-id read bounded to the first 100 rows never saw the current incarnation at all.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the drift is in the NAME MODEL, not in the roster read; a complete roster read still joins nothing. The current incarnation is identified by the unit's MainPID against the name's pid token, a dead one is any offline row that parses under the slot's grammar, and a name outside the grammar stays Foreign. A partial roster must stay unobserved, never a zero.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable (the roster read was bounded and typed, but joined the wrong name). CURRENT: mechanically preventable. A witness plants JIT rows past the first hundred, live and dead incarnations and a stranger, and refuses a join that reads them as the slot's name (test.claim.fleet.fleet_runner_connectivity_witness).",

    "SELECTION ARM NOW EXISTS (P8d, 2026-11-10): the arm the CURRENT rung was missing -- a host-generic selection over ONE complete organization-roster read. gunbc.runner.runner_jit_dead_sweep jit_dead_registration_sweep selects, for a host, every JIT registration that parses under that host's slot grammar (gunbc.runner.runner_incarnation parse_jit_registration_name), is offline, and is not the slot's current incarnation (the unit's MainPID against the pid token); and every registration under a RETIRED name prefix the plan supplies, so a rename's old name (srv4 -> fox) is an input, never a literal. A name that parses against no slot and matches no retired prefix is Foreign and is never selected; the current incarnation is never selected; a partial or unavailable roster read REFUSES rather than reporting a clean sweep (never zero). Its witness plants rows past the first hundred (live, dead, current-incarnation, stranger, retired-prefix) and selects only the dead and the retired-prefix rows. Deletion goes through the one organization runner API route the corpus already uses (gunbc.runner.runner_jit_deregistration ensure_jit_runner_deregistered, reached by gunbc.runner.runner_jit_dead_sweep_run), which lists by name, deletes, and re-reads -- no second client. RUNG, stated to the executed evidence (gunbc.design_argument::guarantee_ladder): the RETIRED-NAME arm is wired live end-to-end (dispatch -> selection -> the one API route, gated on offline + a genuine JIT parse under the retired host's slot instances). The DEAD-INCARNATION arm's SELECTION LOGIC -- offline, parses under the host slot grammar, and is not the slot's current incarnation (the unit's MainPID against the pid token) -- is established by EXECUTED WITNESS EVIDENCE through the real jit_dead_registration_sweep entry (the_current_incarnation_guard_is_load_bearing); its PRODUCTION observation of the per-slot unit MainPIDs is NOT yet wired (ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger: srv4's rename window, P9 -- wiring it reclassifies the read-only dry run to FleetSshKeyConsumed, which the program owner declined for P8d), so the dispatch supplies no MainPIDs today, every offline non-current row reads MainPidUnreadable and is PRESERVED as UNOBSERVED (never a clean zero), and on the executing route only retired-name rows are selected. The WET deletion is gated on the operator's explicit go (its first real use is srv4's rename window, P9); until then only the read-only dry run runs.",

    "CEILING STILL UNCLIMBED: the standing remains below StructurallyGuaranteed. Closing the drift at the root -- deriving the registration-name grammar ONCE from the registering wrapper's own name model so the join and the registrant cannot disagree -- is unbuilt (see trigger_capability); today the sweep and the join still check the grammar declared separately in gunbc.runner.runner_incarnation.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.runner.runner_incarnation", decl_name: "parse_jit_registration_name", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.fleet.fleet_runner_connectivity", decl_name: "decode_registration_slot", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.fleet.fleet_runner_connectivity_witness", decl_name: "a_jit_registration_decodes_to_its_slot_live_or_dead_and_a_stranger_stays_foreign", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.fleet.fleet_runner_connectivity_witness", decl_name: "the_current_jit_incarnation_is_found_by_its_pid_past_the_first_hundred_rows", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.runner.runner_jit_dead_sweep", decl_name: "jit_dead_registration_sweep", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.runner.runner_jit_dead_sweep_run", decl_name: "jit_dead_sweep_deregister", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.runner.runner_jit_dead_sweep_witness", decl_name: "only_dead_and_retired_are_selected_and_the_rest_are_never", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.runner.runner_jit_dead_sweep_witness", decl_name: "a_partial_roster_refuses", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.runner.runner_jit_dead_sweep_witness", decl_name: "the_current_incarnation_guard_is_load_bearing", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.runner.runner_jit_dead_sweep_witness", decl_name: "a_broad_retired_prefix_never_sweeps_a_sibling_host", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.runner.runner_jit_dead_sweep_witness", decl_name: "the_normalised_retired_prefix_sweeps_the_old_host_not_the_srv40_sibling", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.runner.runner_jit_dead_sweep_witness", decl_name: "the_dispatch_input_decoder_is_total_and_fail_closed", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
